looks up to Rudy of the Seven Knights and emulates his fighting style, using a sword in one hand and a shield in the other.\nHe rescued Karin from a group of goblins and formed a team with her. Later, the two stumbled upon a novice adventurer, who was trying to defend people from monsters and they formed a trio.\nEvan despises war and conflict because his friendships with Rudy, Ariel, and Karin, who all lost their parents in war. So, he chose to become an adventurer instead of living a stable life as a soldier.\nHe was eventually chosen by the necklace and has gradually grown into an ally of justice worthy of the title of \"hero.\" He was also sent into the past by the necklace to meet the necklace's former owner, Silvesta, his father, and strives to achieve peace in the world of the past as well."}